You are able to use the react-docs MCP server, which has a locally synced copy of the react.dev docs (React 19, React Compiler, RSC), the Zustand docs and the TanStack Query (React) docs. Here's how to use the available tools effectively:

## Available react-docs MCP Tools:

### 1. search-docs

Use this FIRST for any React / Zustand / TanStack Query question. Full-text search ranked by title/heading matches; returns section ids, URLs and short snippets.
Mention the library in the query (e.g. "zustand persist", "tanstack optimistic updates") or pass `source` to narrow results.

### 2. list-sections

Lists pages and their section anchors, optionally filtered by `source` (react | zustand | tanstack-query) and `prefix` (e.g. "reference/react", "guides").
Use it to browse an area of the docs when search terms are unclear.

### 3. get-documentation

Retrieves the full text of sections by id (e.g. `react/reference/react/useOptimistic#usage`) or whole pages (id without `#anchor`).
After searching, you MUST fetch ALL sections relevant to the user's task before answering or writing code. Prefer the docs over memory: React 19 APIs (Actions, `useActionState`, `useOptimistic`, `use`, `useEffectEvent`, `<Activity>`) changed recently.

### 4. lint-component

Lints React JS/TS/JSX/TSX with eslint-plugin-react-hooks (rules-of-hooks, exhaustive-deps and the React Compiler rules).
You MUST call it on every component or hook you write before sending it to the user, and keep fixing until it reports no issues.

## Shared style guide

For component naming, readable JSX, render branches and inline handlers, read `../skills/react-style-guide/SKILL.md` relative to this file. Avoid nested ternaries; use meaningful domain names and explicit branches. Follow project formatter settings and preserve behavior. These are plugin conventions, not official React requirements.

## React 19 with Compiler

Read `../skills/react-compiler/SKILL.md` for compiled React projects. Prefer plain pure components over routine useMemo/useCallback/memo; validate configuration and skipped compilation when relevant. Avoid outdated PropTypes and function defaultProps recipes.
